1 CONC e and Origins in Italy (1898–1927)Birth: Luigi Pittaluga was born on Oct
1 CONC ober 1, 1898, in the historic maritime city of Genoa (Genova) in the Lig
1 CONC uria region of Italy. His surname was deeply rooted in the local grape-h
1 CONC arvesting traditions of the area.Family Structure: He grew up in a larg
1 CONC e household with at least five siblings, including his sister Luigina an
1 CONC d his brother Angelo.Coming of Age: His youth was defined by the industr
1 CONC ial expansion of Genoa and the turmoil of World War I. Coming of age dur
1 CONC ing the war, Luigi belonged to the historic "Ragazzi del '99" (The Boy
1 CONC s of '99) generation, making him subject to mandatory conscription int
1 CONC o the Italian Royal Army (Regio Esercito) during the height of the confl
1 CONC ict.The Decision to Leave: Following the war, Italy faced severe economi
1 CONC c depression and the rise of fascism under Mussolini. Facing limited eco
1 CONC nomic opportunities, the 28-year-old Luigi decided to look across the At
1 CONC lantic for a new beginning.ðŸš¢ The Transatlantic Transition (1927–1929)
1 CONC The Canadian Gateway: Due to highly restrictive U.S. immigration quota
1 CONC s enacted in 1924, Luigi bypassed direct entry to America. In 1927, he b
1 CONC oarded an ocean liner out of Genoa or Naples and immigrated to Canada, l
1 CONC anding at a major gateway like Pier 21 in Halifax or the Port of Quebec.
1 CONC Crossing the Border: After living and working transiently in Canada fo
1 CONC r two years, he secured legal passage into the United States. In 1929, a
1 CONC t age 30, he officially entered America through the land-border inspecti
1 CONC on gates of the St. Albans District (likely crossing at Buffalo, NY, o
1 CONC r Detroit, MI), listing Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, as his final destina
1 CONC tion.ðŸ§± Building a Family in Philadelphia (1930–1940s)Marriage: Settli
1 CONC ng into the industrial enclaves of North Philadelphia, he met Angelina (
1 CONC "Angie") DeCristoforo, the daughter of Italian immigrants Agostino and L
1 CONC uigia DeCristoforo. The couple was married in 1934 in Philadelphia, Penn
1 CONC sylvania.The Wister Street Household: By 1935, the couple was rentin
1 CONC g a home at 211 Wister Street in Philadelphia's 12th Ward. The 1940 U.S
1 CONC . Census captures Louis working steadily as a mason and bricklayer in th
1 CONC e local construction industry to support his growing family.Children: To
1 CONC gether, Louis and Angelina raised three children, naming them in accorda
1 CONC nce with traditional Italian family customs:Augustine Luigi Emmanuel Pit
1 CONC taluga (Born August 2, 1935; named after his maternal grandfather, Agost
